- content_for :title, "Content decay"
- th_class = "px-3 py-2 font-medium whitespace-nowrap"
- cell_class = "px-3 py-2 text-right whitespace-nowrap tabular-nums"
- rows = @decay.rows

%div{class: "mb-6 flex flex-wrap items-start justify-between gap-3"}
  %div
    %h1{class: "text-2xl font-semibold tracking-tight"} Content decay
    %p{class: "mt-1 text-sm text-slate-500"}
      Entries to update, in one queue: still read though long unchanged, losing the search clicks they had, or slipping down the
      results.
    = last_sync_status("search_console_performance")
  = link_to list_url(@period, @filtering, format: :csv),
    class: "inline-flex items-center gap-1.5 rounded-md border border-slate-300 bg-white px-3 py-1.5 text-sm font-medium text-slate-700 shadow-sm hover:bg-slate-50" do
    = icon("download", size: 14)
    Export CSV

= render "google/shared/period", period: @period, keep: [@filtering]
= search_panel @filtering, keep: [@period]

- unless @decay.compared?
  %p{class: "mb-4 flex items-start gap-2 rounded-lg border border-amber-200 bg-amber-50 px-4 py-3 text-sm text-amber-900", role: "note"}
    = icon("info", size: 16, class: "mt-0.5 shrink-0 text-amber-600")
    %span
      - if @period.compare?
        Search Console wasn't synced for #{@period.previous}, so lost clicks and slipped rankings can't be told yet; only stale
        entries still read are listed.
      - else
        With no comparison, lost clicks and slipped rankings can't be told; only stale entries still read are listed.

- if rows.empty?
  = render "shared/empty_state", message: (@filtering.searching? ? "No entry to update matches." : "Nothing needs updating in this period."), icon: "check-circle"
- else
  %p{class: "mb-3 text-sm text-slate-600"}
    Entries with the most signs first, then the most search clicks lost, the most read in the period, and the longest since an
    update. Stale is unchanged for over #{ContentStats::STALE_AFTER.inspect} yet read #{ContentStats::MIN_VIEWS_TO_REFRESH}+ times.
  %div{class: "relative overflow-x-auto rounded-lg border border-slate-200 bg-white shadow-sm"}
    %table{class: "w-full border-collapse text-sm"}
      %thead{class: "border-b border-slate-200 bg-slate-50 text-slate-600"}
        %tr
          %th{scope: "col", class: "#{th_class} text-right", aria: {label: "Rank"}} #
          %th{scope: "col", class: "#{th_class} text-left"} Entry
          %th{scope: "col", class: "#{th_class} text-left"} Why
          %th{scope: "col", class: "#{th_class} text-right"} Views
          %th{scope: "col", class: "#{th_class} text-right", title: "Clicks from Google Search, Search Console"} Clicks
          %th{scope: "col", class: "#{th_class} text-right", title: "Average position in Google Search"} Position
          %th{scope: "col", class: "#{th_class} text-right"} Updated
      %tbody
        - rows.each.with_index(1) do |row, rank|
          - item = row.item
          %tr{class: "border-t border-slate-100 align-top"}
            %td{class: "px-3 py-2 text-right tabular-nums text-slate-400"}= rank
            %td{class: "px-3 py-2"}
              = blog_page_link(item.entry.name, page_view_path(item.path, **@period.query), live: item.path)
              %span{class: "text-xs text-slate-500"}= item.type.capitalize
            %td{class: "px-3 py-2"}
              %ul{class: "space-y-1"}
                - row.reasons.each do |reason|
                  %li{class: "text-xs text-amber-800"}= reason
            %td{class: cell_class}= number_with_delimiter(item.views)
            %td{class: cell_class}
              = number_with_delimiter(row.clicks)
              - if row.previous_clicks
                %span{class: "block text-xs text-slate-500"} from #{number_with_delimiter(row.previous_clicks)}
            %td{class: cell_class}
              = row.position ? number_with_precision(row.position, precision: 1) : "—"
              - if row.previous_position
                %span{class: "block text-xs text-slate-500"} from #{number_with_precision(row.previous_position, precision: 1)}
            %td{class: "#{cell_class} text-slate-500"}
              = l(item.entry.last_modified_at.to_date)
              %span{class: "block text-xs"}= pluralize(row.age_days, "day") + " ago"
